      <abstract>
        <!-- WHAT
             WHY
             EFFORT
             GOAL
          Gemini:
          Relax-and-Recover (ReaR) is a bash-based disaster recovery framework designed for system administrators to recreate Linux infrastructure following a system failure. By generating a system-specific bootable rescue image paired with automated file restoration workflows, ReaR enables rapid bare-metal recovery and storage layout reconstruction on identical target hardware.
          The following sections describe the general disaster recovery concept and the basic steps you need to execute for successful recovery with &rear;. They also provide guidance on &rear; requirements, some limitations to be aware of, and scenarios and backup tools.-->
        <para><emphasis>Requirements:</emphasis></para>
        <itemizedlist>
          <listitem><para>Two systems: the machine you want to back up, and an identical test machine.
          <quote>Identical</quote> in this context means that you can, for example, replace a network
          card with another one using the same Kernel driver.</para></listitem>
          <listitem><para>Integrated local or third-party backup tool (for example tar, EMC NetWorker, NFS)</para></listitem>
        </itemizedlist>
      </abstract>
